### 2. **Ellipse**
This graph shows an ellipse, demonstrating its shape and key features.

```latex
\begin{tikzpicture}
    \begin{axis}[
        axis lines = middle,
        xlabel = \(x\),
        ylabel = \(y\),
        xmin=-5, xmax=5,
        ymin=-3, ymax=3,
        axis equal,
    ]
    \addplot [
        domain=-4:4,
        samples=100,
        color=blue,
        thick,
    ]
    ({4*cos(x r)}, {2*sin(x r)});
    \addlegendentry{\(\frac{x^2}{16} + \frac{y^2}{4} = 1\)}

    % Foci
    \filldraw (axis cs:3.464,0) circle (2pt) node[below]{Focus};
    \filldraw (axis cs:-3.464,0) circle (2pt) node[below]{Focus};
    \end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
```

### 3. **Parabola**
This graph shows a parabola, highlighting its vertex, focus, and directrix.

```latex
\begin{tikzpicture}
    \begin{axis}[
        axis lines = middle,
        xlabel = \(x\),
        ylabel = \(y\),
        xmin=-5, xmax=5,
        ymin=-1, ymax=9,
        grid=both,
        grid style={line width=.1pt, draw=gray!10},
        major grid style={line width=.2pt,draw=gray!50},
    ]
    \addplot [
        domain=-3:3,
        samples=100,
        color=blue,
        thick,
    ]
    {x^2};
    \addlegendentry{\(y = x^2\)}

    % Vertex
    \filldraw (axis cs:0,0) circle (2pt) node[below left]{Vertex};

    % Focus
    \filldraw (axis cs:0,0.25) circle (2pt) node[right]{Focus};

    % Directrix
    \draw[dashed, red] (axis cs:-5,-0.25) -- (axis cs:5,-0.25) node[right]{Directrix};
    \end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
```

